# StarRocks DDL. Not Ecto, not mix ecto.migrate.
# Apply with the StarRocks SQL console (mysql protocol on FE:9030).
# 0001–0005 are CREATE for a new warehouse; 0006+ are one-shot migrations for
# already-deployed tables. Re-running an ADD COLUMN fails if the column exists.
# 0014 documents, but does not execute, the rebuild an unpartitioned warehouse
# needs, because StarRocks cannot add partitioning or change a primary key with
# ALTER. Its statements are commented out so an in-order apply is a no-op.
# The cnpg_platform JDBC catalog is not here: it is created by
# helm/serviceradar/templates/starrocks-catalog-job.yaml, and the relations it
# may expose are owned by ServiceRadar.Analytics.StarRocks.CatalogAllowlist.
filegroup(
    name = "schema_sql",
    srcs = glob(["*.sql"]),
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)
